{"id":"q44","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"math","question":"Is the 12th Catalan number greater than 200,000?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The 12th Catalan number is C₁₂ = 208,012.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"208,012 is greater than 200,000.","confidence":0.99,"lean":1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The standard indexing of Catalan numbers starts at C₀ = 1.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The formula C_n = (2n)!/((n+1)!n!) gives C₁₂ = 24!/(13!·12!) = 208,012.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The sequence 1, 1, 2, 5, 14, 42, 132, 429, 1430, 4862, 16796, 58786, 208012 confirms the value.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"If 12th is read as an ordinal count starting from C₁, the 12th term is C₁₁ = 58,786.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"58,786 is below 200,000, so the ordinal reading would give NO.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The indexed notation C₁₂ is the usual meaning of 'the 12th Catalan number,' so convention decides in favor of YES.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":-0.8,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":-0.95,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contr